---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro'
import { CONTACT_EMAIL } from '../lib/site'

// Keep this in sync with the site: it is only accurate as long as letzpwn.lu
// stays a static site with no analytics, no cookies and no third-party assets.
const lastUpdated = '15 August 2026'
---

<Layout
  title="Privacy Policy"
  subtitle="Legal"
  description="What data letzpwn.lu processes: no cookies, no analytics, no third-party requests — only the server logs of our host."
>
  <section class="section">
    <div class="auto-container">
      <div class="prose">
        <p class="summary">
          <strong>In short:</strong> letzpwn.lu is a static website. It sets no cookies,
          runs no analytics or tracking, and loads nothing from third-party servers.
          The only data processed when you visit is the request log kept by our hosting
          provider.
        </p>

        <h2>Who is responsible</h2>
        <p>
          LetzPwn asbl, a non-profit association registered in Luxembourg,
          operates letzpwn.lu and is the controller for the data described on
          this page. You can reach us at
          <a href={`mailto:${CONTACT_EMAIL}`}>{CONTACT_EMAIL}</a>.
        </p>

        <h2>What we collect ourselves</h2>
        <p>
          Nothing. The website consists of pre-built HTML, CSS, images and
          fonts. There are no accounts, no forms, no comment system, no
          advertising, and no analytics or tracking scripts of any kind. We do
          not build profiles of visitors and we have no way of recognising you
          across visits.
        </p>

        <h2>Cookies and local storage</h2>
        <p>
          The website sets no cookies and stores nothing in your browser's local
          storage. Because there is nothing to consent to, you will not see a
          cookie banner.
        </p>

        <h2>Third-party content</h2>
        <p>
          Every file the website needs — including the webfonts — is served from
          letzpwn.lu. No embedded fonts, scripts, videos, maps or social media
          widgets contact another company while you read a page, so no third
          party learns of your visit unless you click a link yourself.
        </p>

        <h2>Hosting and server logs</h2>
        <p>
          The website is hosted on GitHub Pages, a service of GitHub, Inc. Like
          any web server, it records technical data about each request in order
          to deliver the page and to keep the service secure and available. That
          typically includes your IP address, the time of the request, the page
          requested, and information your browser sends such as its user agent
          and referring page.
        </p>
        <p>
          These logs are created and controlled by GitHub, not by us — we have
          no access to them and do not receive any statistics from them. GitHub
          is based in the United States; transfers are covered by its own
          safeguards and its
          <a
            href="https://docs.github.com/en/site-policy/privacy-policies/github-general-privacy-statement"
            rel="noopener external"
            target="_blank">GitHub Privacy Statement</a
          >, including the section on
          <a
            href="https://docs.github.com/en/pages/getting-started-with-github-pages/what-is-github-pages#data-collection"
            rel="noopener external"
            target="_blank">data collection by GitHub Pages</a
          >.
        </p>

        <h2>If you contact us</h2>
        <p>
          If you write to us by email, we process your address, your message and
          anything you choose to include, for the sole purpose of answering you.
          We keep such correspondence only as long as it is useful for that
          purpose, and we do not use it for anything else or pass it on.
        </p>

        <h2>Our community platforms</h2>
        <p>
          Our community lives on Discord, and we publish accounts on Twitter/X
          and Instagram. Those are separate services with their own terms and
          privacy policies: when you join or follow us there, the operator of
          that platform processes your data under its own rules, not ours.
          Within our own Discord server we only see what the platform shows any
          server moderator.
        </p>

        <h2>Your rights</h2>
        <p>
          Under the GDPR you have the right to access, rectify and erase your
          personal data, to restrict or object to its processing, and to data
          portability. Since we hold no visitor data, these rights are in
          practice only relevant to correspondence you have sent us — write to
          <a href={`mailto:${CONTACT_EMAIL}`}>{CONTACT_EMAIL}</a> and we will handle
          it. For anything recorded in the hosting logs, please refer to GitHub's
          privacy statement linked above.
        </p>
        <p>
          You also have the right to lodge a complaint with the Luxembourg
          supervisory authority, the
          <a
            href="https://cnpd.public.lu/"
            rel="noopener external"
            target="_blank"
            >Commission nationale pour la protection des données (CNPD)</a
          >.
        </p>

        <h2>Children</h2>
        <p>
          The website is open to everyone and collects no data, so it is safe
          for minors to read. Our community platforms have their own minimum age
          requirements, which we expect members to respect.
        </p>

        <h2>Links to other sites</h2>
        <p>
          Our pages, news posts and writeups link to external websites — CTF
          platforms, challenge write-ups, tools and social media. We have no
          control over those sites and take no responsibility for their content
          or their privacy practices. Their policies apply once you follow a
          link.
        </p>

        <h2>Changes to this policy</h2>
        <p>
          We update this page whenever the way the website works changes. The
          current version is from <strong>{lastUpdated}</strong>; the full
          history is public in the
          <a
            href="https://github.com/LetzPwn/letzpwn-astro"
            rel="noopener external"
            target="_blank">repository of this website</a
          >.
        </p>

        <h2>Contact</h2>
        <p>
          Questions or suggestions about this policy: <a
            href={`mailto:${CONTACT_EMAIL}`}>{CONTACT_EMAIL}</a
          > or via our <a href="/contact">contact page</a>.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>

<style>
  .summary {
    padding: 1.25rem 1.5rem;
    background: var(--lp-surface);
    border-left: 3px solid var(--lp-accent);
    border-radius: var(--lp-radius);
  }
</style>
